    "body": "Correction (SKULL, filer): the worker on PR #1023 found the bug is LATENT, not live - the only Face refusal that carries a spot (`narrow_gap`) needs holes in the region, a turn only comes from an open chain boundary which drops the base face's holes, and any surviving hole is refused first by `face_band_sane` with no spot. So no turned Face refusal reaches the user with a wrong spot today. Decision: keep #1023 as a defensive fix (2 call sites, unit-pinned at π/2 and 3π/2 plus a ghost case) so any future spot-carrying Face refusal lands where the part is. Giving `face_band_sane` a spot is not owed by this issue.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
